# The client grid: one question asked across every client in the practice.
# Each row is a client folder (profile.md plus the documents received so far);
# each column is one question, answered by an agent that cites the passage it
# used, or computed by a formula or a re-runnable check. B-D are the columns a
# practice filters and counts by (return type, status, assignee); E-G give the
# prior-year effective tax rate; H compares the documents each profile expects
# with the files actually in the folder, and re-runs whenever a file under
# clients/ changes; I says whether a "Ready to file" status holds up; J-M read
# QBI and estimated payments; N drafts the request letter for a client who is
# missing something (a ! action: a person runs the first one, then the rest
# can follow). Select B2:M9 and Run Selection to fill the agent cells. The
# clients and documents are synthetic; this shows the board's structure and
# is not tax advice.
instructions = You are a preparer's assistant at a small tax practice, reading one client's folder for the 2025 return. The folder holds profile.md (the engagement: return type, status, assignee, expected documents, estimate plan) and the documents received; the prior-year return summary is the 2024 return. Answer from the files in the folder only. A CORRECTED form replaces the original from the same payer and account. If the files are silent, answer "Not found". Answer in exactly the form the question asks for, with no preamble.
A1 = client folder
B1 = Return type: one of 1040, 1120-S, 1065, 1041
C1 = Status: one of In progress, Waiting on client, Ready to file
D1 = Assignee (first name only)
E1 = Prior-year AGI from the 2024 return summary (for a 1041, its counterpart, adjusted total income; an 1120-S or 1065 has none: answer Not found)
F1 = Prior-year total tax from the 2024 return summary (an 1120-S or 1065: answer Not found)
G1 = Effective tax rate, % (F / E)
H1 = Missing documents (expected in profile.md, not in the folder)
I1 = Status check
J1 = QBI-eligible: does any document show qualified business income for the Section 199A deduction (Section 199A information on an entity return or K-1, Schedule C income, 1099-DIV box 5, or a QBI deduction on the prior-year return)?
K1 = Estimated tax paid for tax year 2025 (the total of the confirmations for tax year 2025; 0 if none)
L1 = Estimated tax planned for 2025 (the annual total in profile.md's plan; 0 if none)
M1 = Behind on estimates
N1 = Request letter (run to draft letters/<client>.md)
A2 = clients/alvarez-reyes/
B2 = @claude('{instructions} Client folder: {$A2}. {B$1}')
C2 = @claude('{instructions} Client folder: {$A2}. {C$1}')
D2 = @claude('{instructions} Client folder: {$A2}. {D$1}')
E2 = @claude('{instructions} Client folder: {$A2}. {E$1}')
F2 = @claude('{instructions} Client folder: {$A2}. {F$1}')
G2 = = if(or({E2} == '', {F2} == ''), '', if(or({E2} == 'Not found', {F2} == 'Not found'), 'n/a', round({F2} / {E2} * 100, 1)))
H2 = $ python3 tools/missing_docs.py {$A2} # watch: clients/**
I2 = = if(or({C2} == '', {H2} == ''), '', if(and({C2} == 'Ready to file', {H2} != 'none'), 'Ready but missing documents', 'ok'))
J2 = @claude('{instructions} Client folder: {$A2}. {J$1}')
K2 = @claude('{instructions} Client folder: {$A2}. {K$1}')
L2 = @claude('{instructions} Client folder: {$A2}. {L$1}')
M2 = = if(or({K2} == '', {L2} == ''), '', {K2} < {L2})
N2 = ! python3 tools/draft_letter.py {$A2} {$H2}
